## Double-Dip Flywheel — How We Train Our Own LLM

### The idea (one paragraph)

We never pay to train on every request. We **speculatively** run two models on the same prompt:

1. **Fast path (local/small)** — default `liquid/lfm-2.5-1.2b-instruct:free`, 8s timeout, resolved from `zie_router_policies` after a fine-tune promotes a LoRA adapter.
2. **Slow path (remote/teacher)** — default `openai/gpt-4o` via OpenRouter (fallback `OPENROUTER_API_KEY_2`).

If the fast model returns **valid JSON** (Zod schema) with **confidence ≥ 0.85**, we serve it and **abort** the slow call — cheap inference, no training row.

If the fast model fails or is uncertain, the slow model runs. When slow wins, we **persist both outputs** to the vault: slow = **chosen** (SFT gold), fast = **rejected** (DPO negative). Over time we fine-tune the 1.2B base so the fast path wins more often — **distilling the teacher into our own weights**.

Implementation: `artifacts/api-server/src/lib/doubleDipRouter.ts` → `executeDoubleDip()`.

### Flow diagram

```
                    POST /manuscript/review
                    POST /seo/audit  (via seoAuditAnalyzer)
                    semanticLegalAnalyzer → captureClauseForVault (shadow)
                    POST /legal/clause/draft (separate path — draftAgent, no race)
                              │
                              ▼
              ┌───────────────────────────────────┐
              │     executeDoubleDip()            │
              │  fast: 1.2B (zie_router_policies) │
              │  slow: gpt-4o (OpenRouter)        │
              │  Zod schema + confidence gate     │
              └───────────────┬───────────────────┘
                              │
            fast wins (conf≥0.85)     slow wins
                    │                      │
                    ▼                      ▼
              return analysis      persistToVault()
              (no vault write)     zie_training_records  (SFT)
                                   zie_preference_pairs  (DPO: chosen/rejected)
                              │
                              ▼ (manual today)
              POST /v1/judge/latest  →  judge_verified, judge_run_id
                              │
                              ▼ (hourly, when thresholds met)
              forgeScheduler → checkThresholdsAndDispatch()
                            → checkVerifiedThresholds()
                              │
                              ▼
              training_jobs (compute_backend=modal)  [needs table LIVE]
              modal.functions train_lora.spawn()
                              │
                              ▼ (webhook / manual)
              updateRoutingPolicy() → zie_router_policies.fast_model_id
                              │
                              ▼
              Next executeDoubleDip() uses fine-tuned LoRA on fast path
```

### Invariants (from code comments)

| ID | Rule |
|----|------|
| INV-02 | Speculative concurrent execution — fast and slow race; slow aborted if fast wins |
| INV-03 | Zod whip — invalid JSON never enters vault |
| — | Vault write **only when slow path wins** (except `draftAgent` / SEO adapter — see below) |
| — | `prompt_hash` SHA-256 dedupes SFT rows (`ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`) |

### Default models

| Role | Default | After fine-tune |
|------|---------|-----------------|
| Fast | `liquid/lfm-2.5-1.2b-instruct:free` | LoRA adapter ID written to `zie_router_policies` |
| Slow (teacher) | `openai/gpt-4o` | Unchanged — continues generating gold labels |
| Confidence gate | `0.85` | Override per caller via `VaultOptions.confidenceThreshold` |

### Task types (free strings — not enum-enforced)

| `task_type` | Vault source | Double-dip? | LIVE status |
|-------------|--------------|-------------|-------------|
| `manuscript_slop_check` | `POST /manuscript/review` | Yes | **PARTIAL** — needs OpenRouter |
| `legal_clause_analysis` | `semanticLegalAnalyzer` shadow hook | Yes (fire-and-forget) | **PARTIAL** — needs `/matter` + KEY_2 |
| `seo_audit` / `seo_content_audit` | `seoFactoryAdapter` / SEO routes | Yes (SEO has own dip in `seo.ts`) | **LIVE** on Railway/Render |
